From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xichen Lin <lukelin0907@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2026 05:04:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] teamd: let the external supervisor own startup timeout

teamd inherited a fixed 20-second daemon startup acknowledgment timeout
from libdaemon's generic example. SONiC startup can legitimately exceed
that limit, after which the child may complete initialization and delete
its newly created team interface when it processes the queued SIGTERM.

Wait without an internal deadline. The SONiC TeamMgr startup helper owns
the bounded 60-second deadline, exact-child termination, reaping, and
cleanup verification.
---
 teamd/teamd.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/teamd/teamd.c b/teamd/teamd.c
--- a/teamd/teamd.c
+++ b/teamd/teamd.c
@@ -1547,2 +1547,2 @@ static int teamd_start(struct teamd_context *ctx, enum teamd_exit_code *p_ret)
-			ret = daemon_retval_wait(20);
+			ret = daemon_retval_wait(0);
 			if (ret < 0) {
